WEBVTT

00:10:00.238 --> 00:10:03.325
Same word, different amount
of remembering; that's weird.

00:10:03.349 --> 00:10:04.992
What's going on here?

00:10:05.016 --> 00:10:10.010
Well, the name Baker
doesn't actually mean anything to you.

00:10:10.034 --> 00:10:14.247
It is entirely untethered
from all of the other memories

00:10:14.271 --> 00:10:15.762
floating around in your skull.

00:10:15.786 --> 00:10:18.940
But the common noun "baker" --
we know bakers.

00:10:19.298 --> 00:10:21.099
Bakers wear funny white hats.

00:10:21.123 --> 00:10:22.726
Bakers have flour on their hands.

00:10:22.750 --> 00:10:25.036
Bakers smell good
when they come home from work.

00:10:25.350 --> 00:10:27.065
Maybe we even know a baker.

00:10:27.089 --> 00:10:28.818
And when we first hear that word,

00:10:28.842 --> 00:10:31.358
we start putting these
associational hooks into it,